QtZpl Aztec encoder

The Aztec placement in src/aztec_encoder.cpp, and
the reference vectors in tests/test_aztec_encoder.cpp, are adapted from
ZXing-C++ v2.3.0, released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Copyright 2016 Huy Cuong Nguyen
Copyright 2016 ZXing authors

Upstream source:
https://github.com/zxing-cpp/zxing-cpp/tree/v2.3.0/core/src/aztec
https://github.com/zxing-cpp/zxing-cpp/blob/v2.3.0/test/unit/aztec/AZEncoderTest.cpp

The high-level character tables and block-selection algorithm are adapted
from OkapiBarcode's AztecCode.java, Apache License, Version 2.0:
Copyright 2014 Robin Stuart
https://github.com/woo-j/OkapiBarcode/blob/365889dd5aea8118cddcc6121aeb6c8a2f7be4d1/src/main/java/uk/org/okapibarcode/backend/AztecCode.java

Modified for QtZpl: standalone QByteArray/std::expected interface; bounded
input; immutable lookup tables; local finite-field arithmetic; ZPL size
selection, reader initialization, ECI, and decimal rune handling. The table
switch emitter replaces the upstream switch tree with explicit mode tables.

There is no dependency on ZXing or OkapiBarcode at build time or runtime.
